### Expected behavior
I expect the Snappy compressor to be able to compress a much larger amount than 32767 bytes.
### Actual behavior
An exception is thrown if the data is too large.
### Steps to reproduce
Try to compress a ByteBuf larger than 32767 bytes using the Snappy.encode method.
### Minimal yet complete reproducer code (or URL to code)
```java
public static void main(String[] args) {
    final byte[] random = new byte[40_000];
    ThreadLocalRandom.current().nextBytes(random);
    { // This should work
        final Snappy snappy = new Snappy();
        final ByteBuf data = Unpooled.wrappedBuffer(Arrays.copyOfRange(random, 0, 32767));
        final ByteBuf out = Unpooled.buffer();
        snappy.encode(data, out, data.readableBytes());
    }
    { // This does not work
        final Snappy snappy = new Snappy();
        final ByteBuf data = Unpooled.wrappedBuffer(random);
        final ByteBuf out = Unpooled.buffer();
        snappy.encode(data, out, data.readableBytes());
    }
}
```
